.SH MINI KEYBOARD REFERENCE
.SS Mini writing desk
.TP
F1 / Esc / q
close help
.TP
↑↓ / j k / PgUp/PgDn
scroll help
.SS Control means Ctrl alone; Command is not required.
.SS Every mode
.TP
Ctrl-S
save
.TP
Ctrl-Q
quit
.TP
Tab
toggle manuscript tree; return to normal
.TP
Ctrl-B
open LOOK clips; insert a numbered clip
.TP
F1
open help without changing mode
.SS Writing panes (outside help)
.TP
W
open split in normal mode or the tree
.TP
Option/Alt-Shift-W
switch writing pane; return to normal
.TP
Ctrl-Shift-W / Ctrl-Option/Alt-W
close focused writing pane; keep other pane and all text
.TP
Ctrl-J / Enter
switch pane in normal writing mode; new line in insert mode
.TP
:only
keep focused pane; hide the other
.TP
:close
close focused pane; keep the other
.SS LOOK Kitty routes pane shortcuts into Mini while it is open. Other terminals must send distinct modified keys; Ctrl-J in normal mode and :close remain available. Closing the only pane leaves it open.
.SS Normal mode
.TP
i / a / o
enter insert mode
.TP
v
enter Vim visual selection
.TP
hjkl / arrows
move
.TP
Ctrl-J / Enter
switch writing pane
.TP
u / Ctrl-R
undo / redo
.TP
x
delete character
.TP
p
paste internal register
.TP
P
open LOOK clips
.TP
0 / $ / G
line start / line end / scene end
.TP
:
enter command
.TP
?
open help
.SS Insert mode
.TP
Type
insert text
.TP
Enter / Ctrl-J
new line
.TP
Backspace / Delete
delete text
.TP
Esc
return to normal
.TP
?
insert a question mark; use F1 for help
.SS Visual selection
.TP
v then arrows / hjkl
extend Vim selection
.TP
y / d
copy / cut Vim selection
.TP
Shift+arrows
start or extend standard selection
.TP
Type
replace a standard Shift selection
.TP
Backspace / Delete
remove a standard Shift selection
.TP
Esc
cancel selection; return to normal
.SS All writing modes
.TP
Arrows
move cursor
.TP
PgUp / PgDn
move a screen; retain screen row and preferred column
.TP
Home / End
line start / end
.TP
Ctrl-Home / Ctrl-End
scene start / end
.TP
Shift + navigation
extend selection
.TP
Ctrl-A
select entire scene
.TP
Ctrl-C / Ctrl-X / Ctrl-V
copy / cut / paste system clipboard
.SS Manuscript tree
.TP
↑↓ / j k
select scene
.TP
Enter
open scene in this pane
.TP
s
add scene at end of selected chapter; start writing
.TP
c
add chapter with Scene 1 at end of book; start writing
.TP
r / R
rename selected scene / its chapter
.TP
Tab
return to writing
.SS Commands
.TP
:w / :wq
save / save and quit
.TP
:q
exit; local recovery files retained
.TP
:split / :sp
open two writing panes
.TP
:only / :close
keep focused pane / keep other pane
.TP
:scene [title]
add scene to current chapter; optional title
.TP
:chapter [title]
add chapter with its first scene; optional title
.SS Titles
.TP
:rename-scene TITLE
rename current scene
.TP
:rename-chapter TITLE
rename current chapter
.SS New chapters, scenes and titles save through Mercury and remain in local recovery if the server is unavailable. Delete is available in the web editor.
.SS LOOK clips stay on this computer. Capture records local copies; it does not sync history across the Fabric. Mini copies/cuts explicitly join this local shelf even with capture off.
